cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "FireScore: a reusable parcel/structure-level wildfire vulnerability index for any US county"
abstract: >-
  FireScore scores every structure in a US county for wildfire vulnerability
  from free national data (OpenStreetMap, USGS 3DEP, LANDFIRE, FEMA USA
  Structures, HIFLD), with egress counted on the real road graph, LANDFIRE
  fuel models, wind-aligned terrain exposure, and structure spacing. One
  online fetch populates a GeoParquet/GeoTIFF cache; every later run is
  fully offline. Scores are reported as ranges across weight-sensitivity
  configurations, and validation against real burn perimeters (permutation
  null, spatial block cross-validation, calibration, and a head-to-head
  against Wildfire Risk to Communities) is built in.
authors:
